---

## 🎯 Key Takeaways

- Identity security is a critical part of enterprise cybersecurity.
- Authentication verifies who you are; authorization determines what you can do.
- MFA adds additional protection against compromised credentials.
- RBAC and least privilege help prevent excessive permissions.
- Active Directory provides centralized identity and access management.
- Domain Controllers handle important authentication and directory operations.
- Privileged accounts require stronger security and continuous monitoring.
- Authentication logs and Windows Event IDs help SOC analysts investigate suspicious activities.
- Proper incident response helps contain compromised accounts and prevent further damage.

> **Remember:**
>
> 👤 IAM manages identities.  
> 🔑 Authentication verifies identities.  
> 🛡️ Authorization controls access.  
> 🏢 Active Directory manages enterprise identities.  
> 📊 Monitoring detects suspicious activities.  
> 🚨 Incident response helps contain security threats.

